KG42.register("rules-0a1b446dcbdd759bb182e60d",{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R010","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-lem","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The local energy product is energy bought from or sold to peers through P2P trading. Scope: P2P trading among prosumers in the proposed local energy market.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"P2P trading among prosumers in the proposed local energy market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-X001","symbol":"P^{pb}_{j,i,t}","meaning":"Energy bought by prosumer j from prosumer i through P2P trading at time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"energy quantity for a peer transaction; sign bounds and unit are not specified in the supplied definition","unit":null,"indices":["j in J","i in J, i != j","t in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R010-X002","symbol":"P^{ps}_{j,i,t}","meaning":"Energy sold by prosumer j to prosumer i through P2P trading at time t.","kind":"operational","domain":"energy quantity for a peer transaction; sign bounds and unit are not specified in the supplied definition","unit":null,"indices":["j in J","i in J, i != j","t in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32"]}],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy product is energy bought from or sold to peers through P2P trading. Scope: P2P trading among prosumers in the proposed local energy market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"In the P2P trading mechanism, a peer transaction is represented by the buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} of prosumer j from prosumer i and the selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} of prosumer j to prosumer i, for distinct prosumers j and i at time t.","expression":"P^{pb}_{j,i,t} \\text{ (buying by } j \\text{ from } i),\\; P^{ps}_{j,i,t} \\text{ (selling by } j \\text{ to } i),\\quad \\forall (j,i)\\in J\\times J,\\; i\\ne j,\\;\\forall t\\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-X001","v141-c-R010-X002"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E32","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M03-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"and the total selling of the P2P trading in each τ so that the re remaining amounts of imports/expor","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The proposed framework incorporates a P2P trading mechanism to facilitate prosumers to trade with their peers. In the proposed P2P trading mechanism, prosumers independently make an optimal decision to buy/sell energy from/to their peers. Moreover, prosumers are able to generate trading amounts and prices optimally for the P2P trading. Let the P2P trading be considered for buying (selling) energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t}(P^{ps}_{j,i,t}) by prosumer j ∈ J from (to) prosumer i ∈ J | i ≠ j."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M03-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"P2P Trading Mechanism","anchor_text":"HOQUE et al.: DOE-BASED LEM FOR PROSUMERS WITH EVs by prosumer j ∈J from (to) prosumer i ∈J |i̸ = j.","equation_id":"(36)-(37)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The single P2P buying energy P^{pb}_{j,i,t} is limited by P^{pb}_{j,t} and the single P2P selling energy P^{ps}_{j,i,t} is constrained by P^{ps}_{j,t} as in (36) and (37), respectively, where P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} is the buying/selling quantity bid of prosumer j at a time t as in Section V-B. Prosumer j can only trade energy with prosumer i at time t as stated in (36) and (37), where C_{j,i,t} is a binary variable to represent the P2P trading status such that C_{j,i,t} = 1 if prosumer j buys energy from prosumer i. 0 ≤ P^{pb}_{j,i,t} ≤ P^{pb}_{j,t} C_{j,i,t}; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T, (36) P^{ps}_{j,t}(1 − C_{j,i,t}) ≤ P^{ps}_{j,i,t} ≤ 0; ∀(j,i) ∈ J | j ≠ i, ∀t∈T. (37)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":"No fixed numeric or unit-bearing parameter is defined in the supplied evidence for this product definition. J and T are index sets used in quantifiers, not theta parameters with source-provided values or units."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-matching","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E32","quote":"In the proposed P2P trading mechanism, prosumers independently make an optimal decision to buy/sell energy from/to their peers."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"2dd6541e82bd27f5f60762e0f6b4130c1405948a2c928b8ca85f27f241fe5860","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The frozen rule defines the local energy product through P2P peer trading. The supplied evidence introduces individual peer buying and selling energy quantities P^{pb}_{j,i,t} and P^{ps}_{j,i,t} for distinct prosumers j and i at time t. These are formalized as source-scoped operational variables belonging to product.local_energy, with a source-supported declaration. No aggregate product equation, sign bounds, or pricing relation is asserted because E32/E33 do not provide one. The original procedural definition is retained unchanged. All cited B evidence remains unreviewed; no independent source audit or scientific acceptance is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-X001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"E32 defines P^{pb}_{j,i,t} as the P2P buying energy by prosumer j from prosumer i, which is a quantity of the local energy product for a peer transaction."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-X002","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"E32 defines P^{ps}_{j,i,t} as the P2P selling energy by prosumer j to prosumer i, which is a quantity of the local energy product for a peer transaction."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The existing procedural core statement defines product.local_energy as energy bought from or sold to peers through P2P trading within the proposed local energy market."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The declaration attaches the source's peer buying/selling energy symbols to product.local_energy. The frozen graph contains no edges for this product definition, so no edge binding is asserted."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
